          "title": "You'll want to know: braquer",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "braquer — \"to turn the wheel (hard); to aim\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Elle a braqué à gauche pour éviter le chat. She turned the wheel hard to the left to avoid the cat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Braquer une banque is slang for to hold up a bank."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of braquer is not fully settled. It is usually traced to a Vulgar Latin verb built on Latin bracchium 'arm' (Lewis & Short): first to point or turn something with the arm."
            }
          ]
        },
