          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "déraper — \"to skid\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Avec la pluie, la voiture a dérapé dans la descente. Because of the rain the car skidded on the way down."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also figurative: la conversation a dérapé — the talk got out of hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "déraper is usually traced to Provençal derapar, first said of an anchor pulled loose from the sea bed, built on a Germanic verb for seizing. EtymDB links it with Germanic cousins such as Old Norse hreppa 'to grasp' (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
