          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "caler in the sense 'to stall' was borrowed from Provençal calar 'to lower a sail', which goes back to Greek khalân 'to slacken' (EtymDB). A boat that lowers its sail stops, and so does an engine."
            }
          ]
        },
